hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2476","Abu Al-Ash’ath reported on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’. He said: Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaqiq, who said: I said to Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform the Duha prayer? She said: “No, unless he comes from the past.” I said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, have a known fast other than Ramadan? She said: “By God, he has never fasted a known month except Ramadan until its time has passed, and he does not break his fast until he has fasted from it.” Mention of the disagreement over Khaled bin Maadan in this hadith"
"2477","Amr bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Baqiya, he said: Buhair told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, that a man asked Aisha about fasting? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast the entire month of Sha’ban, and he sought to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2478","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dawud told us, he said: Thawr told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Rabi’ah Al-Jarashi, on the authority of Aisha, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to fast during Sha’ban and Ramadan, and would strive to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2479","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj reported, on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of Amr bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah, he said: We were with Ammar. Then a praying sheep was brought and he said: Eat. Then some of the people moved away and said: I am fasting. Ammar said: “Whoever fasts on the day of which there is doubt has He disobeyed Abul-Qasim.”"
"2480","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Abu Yunus, on the authority of Simak, I entered upon Ikrimah one day, meaning... Is it more likely to be derived from Ramadan or from Sha`ban? While he was eating bread, beans, and milk, he said to me: Come on, and I said: I am fasting. He said and swore by God: You will break your fast. I said: Glory be to God. Twice, when I saw him swearing without making an exception, I went forward and said, “Bring now what you have.” He said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Fast at the sighting of it and break the fast at the sighting of it. If a cloud or a canopy comes between you and it, then complete the number of days. Sha`ban, and do not face the month facing it, and do not join Ramadan with a day of Sha`ban.”"
"2481","Abd al-Malik ibn Shuaib ibn al-Layth ibn Saad reported, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Shuaib ibn Ishaq told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, and Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he acknowledged that he used to say: “Don’t advance the month by a day or two, except for a man who used to fast, let him fast it.”"
"2482","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his sins will be forgiven.” He came forward from his sin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2483","Muhammad ibn Jabla told me, he said: Al-Mu’afā told us, he said: Musa told us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: He informed me Urwa bin Al-Zubair, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to desire people Regarding standing up for Ramadan without commanding them to do something about it, he says: “Whoever stands up for Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous deeds will be forgiven.” \His sin\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2484","Zakaria bin Yahya reported, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith reported, on the authority of Yunus al-Ayli, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr told me that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the middle of the night and prayed. The mosque and the people prayed. . . . . The chain of the hadith. And in it, he said: He used to encourage them to stand in prayer during Ramadan without ordering them to do so, and he said: “Whoever prays the Night of Decree out of faith And out of hope, he will be forgiven for his previous sins.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and the matter is according to that."
"2485","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah bin told me Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying about Ramadan: “Whoever rises in faith and in expectation of reward will be forgiven.” He will be forgiven for his previous sins.”"
"2486","Muhammad bin Khalid told me, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr informed me, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out in the middle of the night and prayed in the mosque. . . . . He cited the hadith, and said in it: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was urging them to perform the night prayers of Ramadan without ordering them to do anything about it. In it, he says: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2487","Muhammad bin Khalid told me, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abd told me The Most Gracious, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying about Ramadan: “Whoever rises in it out of faith and seeking reward, his sins will be forgiven.” He came forward from his sin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2488","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah told him, Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"2489","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was desirous of praying in Ramadan without ordering them to perform it with determination. He said: “Whoever performs Ramadan with faith... And out of hope, he will be forgiven for his previous sins.”"
"2490","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever prays Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"2491","Muhammad bin Salamah narrated, he said: Ibn al-Qasim narrated, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2492","Muhammad bin Ismail told me, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma told us, he said: Juwayriyah told us, on the authority of Malik, he said Al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah and Humayd bin Abd al-Rahman informed me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who Ramadan rose out of faith and seeking reward. He will be forgiven for all his previous sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2493","Qutayba bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven,” in the hadith of Qutaybah “And whatever is delayed, and whoever performs the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” In the hadith of Qutaibah, “and whatever is delayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2494","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward from Allah, his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2495","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"2496","Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking the reward of reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” Mentioning the disagreement of Yahya ibn Ubay Kathir, and Al-Nadr ibn Shayban is in it."
"2497","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, Muhammad ibn Hisham, and Abu al-Ash`ath narrated, and the wording is his. He said: Khalid narrated to us. He said: narrated to us. Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abu Hurairah told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever stands in Ramadan with faith and in the hope of seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven, and whoever stands in Laylat Al-Qadr with faith and in expectation of reward.” He will be forgiven for his previous sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2498","Mahmoud bin Khalid narrated, on the authority of Marwan, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays the month of Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, will be forgiven for his previous sins.” His sin, and whoever performs the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"2499","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: I am Al-Fadl bin Dukain, he said: Nasr bin Ali, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shayban told me, that He met Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman and said: Tell me the best thing I heard mentioned in the month of Ramadan. Abu Salama said: Abdul told me. Al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he mentioned Ramadan and preferred it over the months, and said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith Seeking reward, he was freed from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is wrong, and what is correct is what we mentioned above. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported, he said: Al-Nadr ibn Shumail narrated to us, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Al-Fadl narrated to us, Al-Nadr ibn Shayban said, on the authority of Abi Salamah, and he mentioned something like it and said: “Whoever fasts and performs it in prayer with faith and seeking reward.”"
"2500","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us Ibn Shayban said: I said to Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman: Tell me about something you heard from your father. Your father heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. There is no one between your father and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the month of Ramadan. He said: Yes, my father spoke to me. He said: The Messenger of God said. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God has enjoined the fast of Ramadan, and He has made it lawful for you to perform it, so whoever fasts it and performs it out of faith and seeking reward, will come out of His sins are like the day his mother gave birth to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2501","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talib, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God says: Fasting is for me and I will reward it for it. And the fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast, and when he meets his Lord, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the scent from the mouth of the fasting person is better to God than the scent of musk.”"
"2502","Muhammad ibn Bashar narrated, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, Abdullah said: God said: “Fasting is for Me and I will reward it, and for the fasting person there are two joys: joy when he meets his Lord, and joy when he breaks his fast, and for the sweetness of the mouth of the fasting person.” “Pleasant to God than the scent of musk.” Mention of the disagreement over Abu Salih in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2503","Ali bin Harb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, he said: Abu Sinan Dirar bin Murrah told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God says: Fasting is for Me and I will reward it. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast he is happy, and when He met God and rewarded him with joy, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2504","Suleiman bin Dawud reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr reported, that Al-Mundhir bin Ubaid narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Samman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “God said: Fasting is for me and I will reward it, and the fasting person rejoices twice: when He breaks his fast, and on the day he meets God, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.”"
"2505","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “There is no good deed that the son of Adam does but that ten good deeds are recorded for him, up to seven hundred times as many. God said: Except fasting. It is mine and I will reward it. He gives up his desires and food for my sake. Fasting is a shield, and the fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy when he breaks the fast. When meeting his Lord, and the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.”"
"2506","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi Al-Maqsimi told me about Al-Masisa, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Juraij said: Ataa told me, on the authority of my father Salih al-Zayyat said that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting.” It is for Me and I will reward for it, and fasting is a shield. If it is a day for one of you to fast, he should not be obscene and should not be noisy, even if someone insults him or fights him. Let him say: I am fasting, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person will be sweeter to God on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk, to the fasting person. There are two joys that make him happy: when he breaks his fast, he rejoices in breaking his fast, and when he meets his Lord, he rejoices in his fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2507","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, a recitation, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ata al-Zayat He heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting. It is for me and I I will reward for it. Fasting is a shield. If it is a day for one of you to fast, he should not be obscene, nor be loud. If anyone insults him or fights him, let him say, “I am A fasting person, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Al-Mubarak is more venerable and higher in our view than Hajjaj, and the hadith of Hajjaj is more worthy of authenticity in our view, and we do not know of a man in the era of Ibn Al-Mubarak. He is more venerable than Ibn Al-Mubarak, nor is he higher than him, nor is he more worthy of every praiseworthy characteristic than him, but there is bound to be a mistake. Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mahdi said: He who acquits himself of error is crazy, but who does not make a mistake? ! The correct thing is: Dhakwan al-Zayyat, not Ata al-Zayyat. This hadith was narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2508","I am Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman. He said: Ibn Wahb told us. He said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. He said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me. He heard Abu Hurairah say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, it is for Me.” And I will reward for it, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2509","Ahmad ibn Issa reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God said: Every good deed that the son of Adam does will receive ten times as much, except fasting, which is for Me.” And I will reward him for it.” Mention of the disagreement over Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub in the hadith of Abu Umamah regarding the virtue of fasting (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2510","Amr bin Ali reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, who said: Mahdi Ibn Maimun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah told me. Ibn Abi Ya’qub, he said: Raja’ Ibn Haywa told me, on the authority of Abi Umamah, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Pass me by. With something I learned from you, he said: “You must fast, for there is nothing like it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2511","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim told me, that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Ya’qub Al-Dhabi He told him, on the authority of Raja bin Haywa, he told him, he said: Abu Umamah Al-Bahili told us, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, instruct me about something that will benefit me. God said: “You must fast, for there is nothing like it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2512","I am Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Da’eef. He said: Ya’qub told us. He said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Ya’qub, on the authority of Abu Nasr, on the authority of Raja bin Haywa, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which work is best? He said: “You must fast, for there is no justice for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2513","Yahya bin Muhammad told me, he said: Yahya bin Kathir told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad al-Dhabi, on the authority of Abu Nasr al-Hilali On the authority of Raja’ bin Haywa, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me to do something. He said: “You must fast, for there is no justice for him.” “I said: O Messenger of God, suggest me to do something.” He said: “You must fast, for there is no justice for him.” I said: O Messenger of God, instruct me to do something. He said: “ You must fast, for there is no justice for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2514","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Samra reported, saying: Al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Fitr, he said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told me, on the authority of Al-Hakam Bin Utaiba, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, who said: Muadh bin Jabal said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a shield.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2515","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit. And Al-Hikam, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Muadh, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a shield.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2516","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of the ruling, he said: I heard Urwa Ibn al-Nazzal narrated, on the authority of Muadh, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a shield.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2517","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj. Shu’bah said: Al-Hakam told me: I heard it from him forty years ago. Then Al-Hakam said Maymun bin Abi Shabib told me about it, and Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj. Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Zayat, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a shield.”"
"2518","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Suwayd reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a reading, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ata. Al-Zayat, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a shield.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2519","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hind, that Mutarrif was a man from Bani Amir bin Sa'sa'ah told him that Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas prayed for him with milk to give him water, and Mutarrif said: I am fasting, so Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Fasting is a protection like the protection of one of you from fighting.”"
"2520","Ali bin Al-Hussein reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adiyy, whose name is Muhammad bin Ibrahim Ibn Abi Adiyy Al-Basri, told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Mutarrif, said: I went to see Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, and he called for milk for me, so I said: I am fasting. He said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a protection from Hell like one of you’s protection from fighting,” Zakaria bin Yahya reported, saying: Abu Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Sa’id Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi Hind said: A mutarrif came to visit Uthman, something like him, as a messenger. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2521","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Wasil told us, on the authority of Bashar bin Abi Saif, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghaytif, Abu Ubaidah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Fasting is a shield unless \He breaks it\"""""""
"2522","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Mushar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Malik, he said: Our companions informed us, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, who said: “Fasting is a shield as long as one does not violate it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2523","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Rahman reported, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “For those who are fasting there is a door in Paradise called: Al-Rayyan. No one will enter it except them. When the last of them enters, it will be closed. Whoever enters it will be closed.” He drinks, and whoever drinks will never thirst.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2524","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: Sahl told me, “In Paradise there is a gate called: Al-Rayyan. It will be said on the Day of Resurrection: Where are the fasting people? Do you have access to Bab al-Rayyan? Whoever enters it never feels thirsty, so when they enter, it is closed for them and they do not enter. There is no one other than them.”"
"2525","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Wahib, who said: Malik and Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever spends two pairs of The path of God will be called out in Paradise: O servant of God, this is good. Whoever is among the people of prayer will be called for the sake of prayer, and whoever is among the people of jihad. He was called from the gate of jihad, and whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity, and whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of Rayyan,” he said. Abu Bakr: O Messenger of God, is there any necessity for anyone to be called through those gates? Is anyone invited from all those doors? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them.”"
"2526","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were young and unable to do anything, so he said: “Oh Young people, you must abstain from fasting, for it lowers the gaze and improves chastity. Whoever is not able to do so should fast, for it is for him. \And he came\"""""""
"2527","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far informed us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah said that Ibn Masoud met Uthman at Arafat and was alone with him. He told him that Uthman said to Ibn Masoud: Do you have a girl that I can marry to you? So Abdullah called Alqamah and it was narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you is able to do so, let him get married, for he is more likely to “For sight and protection of chastity, and whoever is not able, let him fast, for fasting is a reward for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2528","Harun bin Ishaq reported, he said: Al-Muharbi reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Whoever of you can afford it, let him get married, and whoever cannot find it must fast.” For it has come.”"
"2529","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid said: We entered upon Abdullah and with us was Alqamah, the lions, and a group. He narrated to us a hadith that I had not seen him narrate. The people, except for my sake, because I was the youngest of them in age. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O young people, who among you is able So, let him get married, for it is more pleasing to one’s gaze and a better part of one’s chastity.” Ali said: Al-A’mash was asked about the hadith of Abraham, and he said: About Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah: The same, and he said: Yes."
"2530","Amr bin Zurarah reported, he said: Ismail reported, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah said: I was with Ibn Masoud and he was with Uthman, and Uthman said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to meet Ali, meaning a young man. He said: “Whoever among you has longevity, let him get married, for it will be more tender for the eyes and more secure for chastity, and whoever is not, then fasting will be a reward for him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Abu Ma`shar, whose name is Ziyad bin Kulayb, is trustworthy, and he is the companion of Ibrahim. Mansour and Mughirah narrated on his authority. Shu`bah, and Abu Ma`shar al-Madani. His name is Najih, but he is weak, and in addition to his weakness, he had mixed objectionable hadiths. From her"
"2531","Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Between the east and the west is a qibla.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2532","Among them is Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not cut meat with a knife, but tear it apart.” \Nahsha\"" and other than that (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2533","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed me, he said: Anas, Ibn Iyadh, told me, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever fasts a day for the sake of God, God will remove his face from the Fire on that day for seventy days.”"
"2534","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Suhail bin Abi told me Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts a day in the way of God, God will distance his face from the Fire for seventy days.”"
"2535","Dawud bin Sulaiman bin Hafs reported, Abu Muawiyah Al-Dareer said: On the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever fasts a day for the sake of God, God will distance him from Hell on that day for seventy days,” he said. Abu Abdul Rahman: This is a mistake. We do not know of anyone who followed Abu Muawiyah on this chain of transmission."
"2536","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Safwan, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever fasts a day for the sake of God, God will remove his face from Hell for seventy years.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2537","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Ibn Abu Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no servant who fasts a day in the path of God, except On that day, God will keep his face away from the Fire for seventy days. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2538","Al-Hasan bin Qaza’ah reported, on the authority of Humaid bin Al-Aswad, who said: Suhail told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts a day for the sake of God, God will keep his face away from Hell for seventy years.”"
"2539","Mu’mal bin Yahab told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Yahya bin Sa’id and Suhail bin told me. Abu Salih, they heard Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, saying: I heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: : “Whoever fasts a day in the cause of God, God will keep his face away from the Fire for seventy days.” Mention of the disagreement over Sufyan Al-Thawri regarding it."
"2540","Abdullah bin Munir narrated, he said: Yazid Al-Adani narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abu Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No servant fasts a day in the path of God, unless he By God, on that day, the Fire will descend from his face for seventy days.”"
"2541","Ahmad bin Harb reported, saying: Qasim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts a day in the path of God, God will thereby remove the heat of Hell from his face.” \seventy autumns\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2542","Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, he said: I read to my father, he said: Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Sumayy, On the authority of Al-Numan bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts a day in the path of God On that day, God removed the Fire from his face for seventy days.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He was named a servant of Abu Bakr ibn Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham Al-Madani, Malik narrated from him, and Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan said: Al-Qaqa’ ibn Hakim is the most beloved To me than Sumayy, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Both of them are trustworthy to me, and Sumayy is more beloved to us than Suhail bin Abi Saleh."
"2543","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shuaib, he said: Yahya bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim Abi Abdul Rahman that He narrated to him, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever fasts a day in the path of God, God will keep Hell away from him.” A hundred years' journey (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2544","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Safwan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, on the authority of Ka’b bin Asim said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “It is not righteous to fast while traveling.”"
"2545","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is wrong, and we do not know of anyone who followed it. Muhammad ibn Kathir has this chain of narration, and God knows best, and the authentic hadith that preceded it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2546","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw people gathered around a man, so he asked, and they said: A man exhausted by fasting, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “It is not righteous to fast while traveling.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2547","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Saeed told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, He said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Jabir bin Abdullah told me, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He passed by a man in the shade of a tree, sprinkling water on him. He said: “What is the matter with this friend of yours?” They said: O Messenger of God, he is fasting. He said: “It is not righteous for you to fast while traveling, and you have the permission of God which He has granted you, so accept it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Wrong. Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman did not hear this hadith from Jabir. Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Faryabi told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman, he said: I was told by someone who heard Jabir similar to him mentioning the disagreement over Ibn al-Mubarak regarding him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2548","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: Waki` informed me, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed me, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not righteous to fast while traveling. God’s permission is upon you, so accept it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2549","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Uthman ibn Umar, who said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd. The Most Gracious, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not righteous to fast while traveling.” Mention of the man’s name (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2550","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Yahya and Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Amr bin Hassan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man who had shadowed him while travelling, and he said: “ It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith of Shu’bah is authentic. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2551","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Ja`far bin Muhammad, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Mecca in the year of the conquest in Ramadan, and he fasted until he reached the size of the clouds. So the people fasted, but he heard that the people had found it difficult to fast, so he called for a cup of water after the afternoon prayer and drank while the people were watching, so some of them broke their fast. The people, and some of them fasted, then he heard that some people had fasted, so he said: “Those are disobedient.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2552","Harun bin Abdullah and Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with the dates of Dhahran for lunch, and he said: To Abu Bakr and Omar: “Come and eat.” They said: We are fasting. He said: “Go to your companion and work for your companion.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake. We do not know that anyone followed Abu Dawud on this narration, and what is correct is mursal. Imran bin Yazid informed me, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib informed me, he said: Al-Awza’i informed me, on the authority of Yahya that he told him, on the authority of my father Salamah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down from Dhahran, on a mission. Mahmoud bin Khaled told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He was having lunch with the dates of Dhahran, and with him were Abu Bakr and Omar. He said: “Lunch” as a messenger. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, saying: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar was in Murr al-Dhahran, sent as a messenger. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2553","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shuaib, he said: Al-Awza’i informed, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Amr bin Umayyah Al-Damri told me, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from a journey, and he said: “Wait for lunch, Abu Umayyah.” I said: I am fasting. He said: “Come near me so I can tell you about the traveler. Indeed, God has exempted fasting from him and half of the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2554","Amr ibn Qutaibah informed us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir told me, he said: He told us Abu Qalaba, he said: Ja’far bin Amr bin Umayyah Al-Damari told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked me: “Aren’t you waiting for lunch, O Abu Umayyah?” I said: I am fasting. He said: “Come, I will tell you about the traveler. God has placed on his behalf\"","" meaning: fasting and half of the prayer."""""
"2555","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Umayyah Al-Damari said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from a journey, and I greeted him. When I went out, he said: “Wait for lunch.” “O Abu Umayyah,” I said: “I am fasting, O Prophet of God.” He said: “Come, I will tell you about the traveler. Indeed, God has exempted fasting from him and half of the prayer.” Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, Musa bin Marwan told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abu Qalaba told me, he said: Abu Al-Muhajir told me, he said: Abu Umayyah told me, that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he mentioned something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2556","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abu Qalaba al-Jarmi told me, that Abu Umayyah al-Dhamri told them, that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him He greeted someone from a journey and said: “Wait for lunch, O Umayyah.” I said: I am fasting. He said: “Come, I will tell you about the traveler. Indeed, God has forbidden from him Fasting, and half of the prayer.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an error. His saying: Abu Umayyah told them a mistake. This saying He himself mentioned the disagreement between Muawiyah bin Salam and Ali bin Al-Mubarak in this hadith."
"2557","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Yazid bin Ibrahim Al-Harrani reported, saying: Uthman told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, that Abu Umayyah told him that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from a journey while he was fasting, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Aren’t you waiting for lunch?” He said: I am fasting. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Come, I will tell you.” Regarding fasting, God has removed from the traveler fasting and half of the prayer.” Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, saying: Uthman ibn Umar told us, he said: Ali reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of a man, that Abu Umayyah informed him, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Travel, etc (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2558","I am Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan. He said: My father told us. He said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has removed from the traveler, meaning: half of the prayer and fasting, and from the pregnant and breastfeeding woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2559","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of a sheikh from the Banu Qusayr, on the authority of his uncle, he told us, he said: Then they met him with his camels, and Abu Qalaba said to him, “Tell him,” and the Sheikh said, “My uncle told me that he He went with his camels and came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was eating, or he said: eating, and he said: “Come near, and eat,” or he said: Come and feed.” So I said: I am fasting. He said: “God has removed half of the prayer and fasting from the traveler, and from the pregnant and breastfeeding woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2560","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Suraij told me, he said: Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Abu Bakr told me Qilabah, this hadith. Then he said: Do you have a word about the author of the hadith? He directed me to him, and I met him. He said: A relative of mine, called Anas bin Malik, told me: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in search of camels for a neighbor of mine. I took it, so I sat with him while he was eating, so he invited me to his food, and I said: I am fasting. He said: “Come, let me tell you about that. Indeed, God has put The traveler: fasting and half of the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2561","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Khaled al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of a man, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him for a need, then he was having lunch, and he said: “Come to lunch,” and I said: I am fasting, and he said: “Come, I will tell you about fasting.” “Half of the prayer and fasting has been waived from the traveler, and a concession has been granted to the pregnant and the breastfeeding woman.” Suwayd reported, saying: Abdullah reported, about Khaled, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of the man, and something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2562","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Hani bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of a man from the tribe of Al-Harish. On the authority of his father, he said: I was traveling, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was fasting, and he was eating. He said: “Come on.” I said: I am fasting. He said: “Come, do you not know what God has set aside for the traveler?” He said: “Fasting and half the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2563","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, On the authority of Hani bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of a man from Banu Al-Huraish, on the authority of his father, he said: We were traveling and we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him while he was eating, and he said: “Come and eat.” I said: I am fasting, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will tell you about fasting. “Indeed, God has removed from the traveler fasting and obligatory prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2564","Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Karim told us, he said: Sahl bin Bakkar told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Hani bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of his father, said: I was traveling and I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was eating while I was fasting, and he said: “Come on.” I said: I am fasting. He said: Do you know what God has withheld from the traveler? I said: And what He has removed from the traveller. He said: Fasting, and half of the prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2565","Ahmad bin Suleiman reported, saying: Ubayd Allah told us, saying: Israel reported, on the authority of Musa, who was the son of Abi Aisha, on the authority of Ghaylan, He said: I went out with Abu Qalaba on a journey, and he brought food. I said: I am fasting. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on a journey, and he brought food. His food, so he said to a man: “Come and eat.” He said: I am fasting. He said: “God has removed from the traveler half of the prayer and fasting while traveling, so come.” So he fed. So I approached and fed"
"2566","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated, he said: Asim Al-Ahwal narrated to us, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijli, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. Some of us were fasting and some were breaking the fast. We camped on a hot day and took shade. Fasting, and those who broke their fast stood up and gave the passengers water, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Today those who broke their fast have gone with their reward.”"
"2567","Muhammad bin Aban reported, saying: Ma’an told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: “It is said: Fasting while traveling is like breaking the fast while at home.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an error. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2568","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hammad al-Khayat told us, and Abu Amir al-Aqdi told us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, said: “The fasting person while traveling is like the one who breaks the fast while at home.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2569","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Awf, on the authority of his father, said: “One who fasts while traveling is like one who breaks his fast while at home.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2570","Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He went out during Ramadan and fasted until he came a long time ago, and he brought a cup of milk and drank, and he broke his fast.” And his companions\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2571","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi reported, saying: Sa’id bin Amr told us, he said: Abthar told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted from Medina until he came shortly before, then He broke his fast until he reached Mecca.” The disagreement with Mansour was mentioned regarding it."
"2572","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Mecca and fasted until Usfan came and called for a cup and drank. He said: Shu’bah in Ramadan, so he was Ibn Abbas says: Whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break his fast."
"2573","Muhammad bin Qudamah reported, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God traveled May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Ramadan, so he fasted until he reached Usfan, then he called for a vessel and drank during the day, and the people saw him, then he broke his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2574","Humaid bin Masada reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, he said: I said to Mujahid: Fasting while travelling? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on it and break his fast.”"
"2575","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, he said: he told us Mujahid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “fasted during the month of Ramadan and broke his fast while traveling.”"
"2576","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated, saying: Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting while travelling. He said: “If.” Then he mentioned a word that means If you wish, you may fast, and if you wish, you may break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2577","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith and Al-Layth told me, and another mentioned, on the authority of Bukayr, On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami, he said: O Messenger of God, I find the strength to fast while traveling. He said: “If you wish So fast, and if you wish, break your fast.” Qutaybah bin Sa’id reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, that Hamza Bin Amr, he said: O Messenger of God, someone like him is a messenger."
"2578","Anba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting while traveling. He said: “If you want, fast, and if Whatever you wish, break your fast"
"2579","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting while travelling. He said: “If “If you want to fast, then fast, and if you want to break the fast, break the fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2580","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Abdul Hamid bin Jafar told us, he said: he told me Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Fasting while traveling. He said: “If you want to fast, then fast, and if you want to break your fast, then break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2581","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Suleiman bin Left, and Hanzala bin Ali, he said: They all told me, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr, he said: I used to narrate fasting during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. I said: O Messenger of God, I used to fast regularly. Should I fast while travelling? He said: “If you want, then fast, and if you want, then break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2582","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Imran bin Abu Anas, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Ali, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr, he said: I said: O Prophet of God, I am a man who regularly fasts. Should I fast while traveling? He said, “If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2583","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`d reported, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Imran ibn Abi Anas told me, that Suleiman bin Yassar narrated to him, that Abu Marawahih narrated to him, that Hamza bin Amr narrated to him, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was a man who fasted. I would fast while travelling. He said: “If you want, then fast, and if you want, then break your fast.”"
"2584","Anba Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr told us, and another mentioned, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Abu Mawwih, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr, that he said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I find in myself the strength to fast while traveling, so is there a sin on me? He said: “It is a concession from God, so whoever takes it will do well, and whoever loves to fast is not guilty of sin.”"
"2585","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami, he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, should I fast while travelling? He said: “If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break your fast.” He mentioned the disagreement over Hisham bin Urwa regarding it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2586","Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Lani Al-Kufi reported, saying: Abd al-Rahim reported, saying: Hisham told us, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr, that he said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who fasts. Should I fast while travelling? He said: “If you want, then fast, and if you want, then break your fast.”"
"2587","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim told us, saying: Malik told me, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of God, should I fast while travelling? He used to fast a lot, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “If you want, fast, and if you want, break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2588","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: Hamzah asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, should I fast while travelling? He said: “If you want, then fast, and if you want, then break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2589","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah bin Sulayman told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Hamza asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, O Messenger of God, should I fast while travelling? He said: “If you want, then fast, and if you want, then break your fast.”"
"2590","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdah bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Hamza Al-Aslami asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting while travelling? He was a man who recounted fasting, so he said: “If you want, fast, and if you want, break your fast.” Mention of the disagreement over Abu Nadhrah al-Mundhir ibn Malik ibn A piece"
"2591","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Should I fast while travelling? He said: “If you want, then fast, and if you want, then break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2592","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi narrated, saying: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, he said: Abu Saeed narrated to us, He said: “We used to travel during Ramadan, and some of us would fast and some of us would break the fast. The fasting person does not blame the one who broke the fast, nor does the one who broke the fast blame the fasting person.”"
"2593","Sa`id bin Ya`qub al-Talqani reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Maslama, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, he said: “We were traveling with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Among us is the fasting person and among us is the one who breaks the fast, and the fasting person does not blame the one who breaks the fast, nor does the one who breaks the fast blame the fasting person.”"
"2594","Abu Bakr bin Ali reported, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Bishr bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Nadra On the authority of Jabir, he said: “We traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some of us fasted and some of us broke our fast.”"
"2595","Ayoub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan told me, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah Al-Mundhir, who is the son of Malik bin Al-Basri’s quotation, on the authority of Abu Sa’id and Jabir bin Abdullah, that they traveled with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “So the fasting person fasts and breaks his fast.” The one who breaks the fast, the fasting person does not blame the one who breaks his fast, nor does the one who breaks the fast blame the fasting person.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, his name is Saad bin Malik. Ibn Sinan, Abu Talha Al-Ansari’s name is Zayd ibn Sahl, and Abu Ayyub’s name is Khallad ibn Yazid. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2596","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the year of the conquest, fasting during Ramadan until, when he was in difficulty, he broke his fast.”"
"2597","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal, meaning Ibn Muhalhalil, narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled and fasted until he reached Usfan, then he called for a vessel and drank during the day. So that the people could see him, then he broke his fast until he entered Mecca, so he opened Mecca in Ramadan. Ibn Abbas said: “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted in He traveled and broke his fast. Whoever wished may fast, and whoever wished may break his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is wrong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2598","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Wahb bin Khaled, he said: Abdullah bin Sawada told us Al-Qushayri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, a man from among them, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Medina while he was having lunch, and he said The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him: “Come to lunch.” He said: I am fasting. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Indeed, God has put “For the traveler, fasting, half of the prayer, and for the pregnant and breastfeeding woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2599","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Yazid, the servant of Salamah ibn al-Akwa’, on the authority of Salamah ibn al-Akwa’, said: “When this verse was revealed, and those who are able to do it must pay a ransom by feeding a poor person, there were He wanted us to break the fast and make a ransom until the next verse was revealed and abrogated it.”"
"2600","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Warqa’ informed, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: And those who are able to bear it must pay a ransom by feeding a poor person. A poor person: one, so whoever volunteers: it increases the food of another poor person, it is not abrogated, it is better for him, and that you fast is better for you: no. This is permitted except for an elderly person who cannot tolerate fasting or a sick person who cannot recover.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2601","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ali bin Mushar reported, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muadha al-Adawiya, that a woman asked Aisha, can a menstruating woman perform the prayer when she becomes pure? She said: “Are you a female slave? We used to menstruate during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we would purify ourselves and he would order us to make up for the fast, and we would not He commands us to make up the prayers.”"
"2602","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah talking, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “If I have to fast from Ramadan, then I will not make it up until Shaaban comes.”"
"2603","Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus reported, saying: Abthar narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Saifi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Ashura: “Has any of you eaten anything today?” So they said: Who among us has fasted, and who among us has eaten? He did not fast. He said: “So complete the rest of your day, and send for the people of the offerings and let them complete the rest of their day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2604","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Salamah told us, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said For a man: “On the day of Ashura, whoever has eaten may complete the rest of his day, and whoever has not eaten may fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2605","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Asim bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me one day and said: “Do you have anything?” So I said: No. He said: “I am fasting.” Then he passed by me after that day, and Hais had been given to us as a gift, so I hid some of it for him, and he loved Hais. I said: O Messenger of God, it was given as a gift. We have some food, so I hid some of it for you. He said: “Come close to it, but this morning I am fasting.” So he ate some of it, then he said: “It is just like fasting.” Voluntary action is like a man who gives charity from his wealth. If he wishes, he gives it, and if he wishes, he withholds it.”"
"2606","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sharik reported, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned around and said: “Do you have anything?” I said: I do not have anything. He said: “So I am fasting.” She said: Then he came to me the second time, and some wheat had been given to us as a gift, so I brought it. He said: “As for me, I have started fasting.” He ate, and I was amazed at him. So I said: O Messenger of God, you entered upon me while you were fasting, and then you ate goats? He said: “Yes, O Aisha, she is in the same position as someone who fasts other than Ramadan, or in making up for Ramadan, or in voluntary prayers, in the same position as a man who goes out. He gave his money as charity, so he took from it whatever he wanted, so he spent it and was stingy with what was left, so he withheld it.”"
"2607","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come and say: “Do you have lunch?” So we would say: No, and he would say: “I am He is fasting. One day he came to us and Hais was given to us as a gift. He said: “Do you have anything?” We said: Yes, Hais was given to us as a gift. He said: “As for the morning... I want to fast,” so he ate"
"2608","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Aisha, daughter of Talha, On the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us one day and we said: Give us some living things, of which we have made for you. share, so he said: “I am fasting,” so he broke his fast."
"2609","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Talha bin Yahya told us, he said: Aisha bint Talha told me, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to her while he was fasting, and he said: “Do you have anything to feed me in the morning?” So we say: No, so he says: “I am fasting.” Then he came to her after that, and she said: “A gift was given to us.” He said: “What is it?” She said: “Hays.” He said: “It may be.” “I am fasting in the morning,” so he ate (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2610","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Waki’ narrated, he said: Talha bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of his paternal aunt Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me one day and said: “Do you have anything?” We said: No, he said: “So I \fasting\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2611","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Ma’n, he said: Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, and Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to her and said: “Do you have “Food?” I said: No. He said: “I am fasting.” Then another day came and Aisha said: O Messenger of God, Hais was given to us as a gift. So they called for it. He said: “As for me, I have been fasting in the morning,” so he ate. Anba Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu’afa bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid. And Umm Kulthum, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Aisha and said: “Do you have food?” and the like. Abu Abdul Rahman said: It was narrated by Samak bin Harb, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha"
"2612","Safwan bin Amr told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, he said: he told me A man, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, Mother of the Believers, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day and said: “Did “Do you have any food?” I said: “No.” He said: “Then I will fast.” She said: “Then he came in again and I said: “Hays has been given to us as a gift.” He said: “Then I will break my fast.” Today I have made obligatory fasting.”"
"2613","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar reported, saying: Sa`id bin Sharhabeel told us, saying: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever does not spend the night fasting before dawn, there is no fasting for him.”"
"2614","Abdul-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad reported, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever does not spend the night fasting before dawn, there is no fasting for him.”"
"2615","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Ashhab, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told me, and another mentioned, that Abd Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm told them, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not complete the fast before dawn comes, may not fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2616","Ahmad ibn Al-Azhar reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hafsa, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not spend the night fasting, there is no fasting for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2617","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Mu`tamar told us, saying: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abdullah, On the authority of Hafsa, she used to say, “Whoever does not complete the fast during the night must not fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2618","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no fasting for the one who does not gather before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2619","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Isa, who is Ibn Masargis, told us, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak reported, he said: Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: “There is no fasting for one who does not He gathers before dawn.”"
"2620","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: “There is no fasting for the one who does not complete the fast before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2621","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Hafsa, “No Fasting for those who did not complete the fast before dawn.”"
"2622","Ahmad bin Harb Al-Mawsili reported, saying: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: “No Fasting for one who does not perform the prayer before dawn.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: What is correct in our view is suspended, and it is not valid to raise it, and God knows best. Because Yahya bin Ayyub is not that strong, and the hadith of Ibn Jurayj on the authority of Al-Zuhri is not preserved, and God knows best, Malik sent him"
"2623","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Aisha and Hafsa, “like no “He fasts except those who have completed the fast before dawn.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said that he used to say: No. He who has completed all fasts before dawn shall fast."
"2624","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: “He does not fast Except for one who completes the fast before dawn.”"
"2625","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, saying: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “If A man combines fasts during the night and does not fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2626","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, that he heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most beloved of God is the fasting of David. He used to fast one day and break his fast.” One day, and the most beloved prayer to God was the prayer of David. He used to sleep at midnight, a third of it he would wake up, and a sixth of it he would sleep.”"
"2627","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is the son of Musa, told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not break the fast on the days of whiteness while he was home or travelling.”"
"2628","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to fast so that we say: he would not break his fast, and he would break his fast so we say: he did not want to fast, and he did not fast for a month.” “There has been no Ramadan in a row since the arrival of Medina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2629","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar al-Marwazi narrated, saying: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Marwan Abi Lubaba, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He fasts until we say: He does not want to break his fast, and he breaks his fast until we say: He does not want to fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2630","Ismail bin Masoud narrated, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Saeed narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I do not know that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the entire Qur’an in one night, and did not stand up until the morning. He has never fasted a full month other than Ramadan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2631","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aisha about the Prophet’s fasting. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: “He used to fast so that we would say that he had fasted, and he would break his fast so that we would say that he had broken his fast, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not fast.” And he gave peace for a whole month since he came to Medina, except Ramadan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2632","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Mu’awiyah bin Salih reported that Abdullah bin Abi Qays told him. He heard Aisha say: “The most beloved of the months to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to fast in Sha`ban. Rather, he used to pray in it.” \In Ramadan\"""""""
"2633","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Malik told me, and Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and another one before them mentioned that Abu Al-Nadr He told them, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast until we say that he does not break his fast, and he would break his fast until We say that he does not fast, and I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complete the fast of any month except Ramadan, and I have never seen the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in A month with more fasting than in Sha`ban.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2634","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not fast for two consecutive months except Sha’ban. And Ramadan"
"2635","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Basri al-Busri reported, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, about the repentance of Huw al-Anbari, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “he did not fast a complete month of the Sunnah except Sha`ban.” Ramadan will continue with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2636","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad reported, saying: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Tell me Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not fasting more during a month than this. For Sha`ban, he used to fast it or not.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2637","Amr bin Hisham reported, saying: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast in Sha`ban except for a short time.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2638","Amr bin Uthman reported on the authority of Baqiya, saying: Buhair told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, that Aisha said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast the entire month of Sha’ban.”"
"2639","I am Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Thabit bin Qais Abu Al-Ghusn, a sheikh from the people of Medina, narrated to us. He said: Abu Al-Ghusn narrated to me. Saeed Al-Maqbari, he said: Usama bin Zaid told me, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have not seen you fast as many months in a month as you do in a month. Sha`ban, he said: “That is a month that people ignore between Rajab and Ramadan, and it is a month in which deeds are submitted to the Lord of the worlds, so I love That my deeds will be lifted while I am fasting.”"
"2640","I am Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Thabit bin Qais Abu Al-Ghusn, a sheikh from the people of Medina, narrated to us. Abu Saeed narrated to me. Al-Maqbari, he said: Usama bin Zaid told me, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, you fast until you can hardly break your fast, and you break your fast until you can barely break your fast. You fast except for two days if they fall within your fast, otherwise you fast on them. He said: “Which two days?” I said: Monday and Thursday. He said: “Which two days?” Those are two days in which deeds are presented to the Lord of the Worlds, so I would like for my deeds to be presented while I am fasting.”"
